(ns cohost.region-eve
  "jank-seat hosting for the region leaves (Eve-in-cohost unit 6,
   doc/eve-cohost/UNIT6-DESIGN.md sections 3b and 7.5): Eve's own region
   adapter, installed as the host adapter's :region-open / :region-heap /
   :region-sync leaves.

   jank-only (.jank) and loaded only where Eve's jank realization is on the
   module path (`bb classpath jank` in an Eve checkout whose :jank row is
   native); nothing in cohost's shim or boot requires it -- the shape of
   cohost.http-eve and cohost.memory-eve on the JVM seat. The leaves are
   Eve's exports exactly: eve.region/open-mmap-region,
   eve.region/make-heap-region, eve.mem/sync-region!. cohost adds no region
   and no operation of its own (MEMORY-PLAN.md section 9); Eve's jank region
   adapter exports no close, so there is no close leaf.

   cohost.object-eve is required first: it loads Eve's core completion -- on
   jank, Eve's namespaces load only after it, since it interns deftype,
   defprotocol, ... into clojure.core, seen only by namespaces created after
   it (Eve's own launcher, test/eve/runner/jank_main.jank, requires it first)
   -- and gives the completion cohost's object, so the regions Eve makes here
   are cohost objects with Eve's tag (unit 6 step 2, design section 3a). The
   completion also re-roots clojure.core names (defn, fn, let, =, hash,
   deref, ...) for every namespace compiled after it; cohost's jank host is
   loaded before it (cohost.object-eve requires it), and cohost's battery
   and libraries with the completion loaded measured 219/221 and 62/62
   (design section 8.4)."
  (:require [cohost.object-eve]
            [cohost.adapter :as adapter]
            [eve.mem :as eve-mem]
            [eve.region :as eve-region]))

(defn install!
  "Install Eve's region leaves over the current host adapter. Returns
   whether the seat now has regions."
  []
  (adapter/install! (assoc (adapter/current)
                           :region-open eve-region/open-mmap-region
                           :region-heap eve-region/make-heap-region
                           :region-sync eve-mem/sync-region!))
  (adapter/regions?))
